(scans a lathe polyline's offset profile for the first above-to-below)
(transition - the profile dropping back below a roughing level, i.e.)
(re-entering safe-to-cut territory - that occurs strictly past search_from.)
(Used by poly_lathe_mill's disjoint-interval roughing to find a further)
(interval to cut at the SAME level, after lathe_level_pass stopped earlier)
(in the window - successfully, or blocked - because the profile rose back)
(above the level - a re-entrant profile can do that more than once.)
(Deliberately NOT a copy of lathe_level_pass's scan with the inequality)
(flipped: that scan's gate stops testing the moment ANY crossing is found,)
(which is correct there since the first-in-array-order match IS the answer.)
(Here the first match in array order can be BEFORE search_from - e.g. the)
(very joint search_from itself came from - and must be rejected while the)
(scan keeps going, so the loop's continue-condition is keyed on a genuinely)
(qualifying match, not on "any match at all".)
(CALL pds[1] level[2] floor_off[3] search_from[4] w_to[5])
(outputs: #<_pl_resume_found> - 0 or 1 - and #<_pl_resume_z>)
o<lathe_level_next_start> sub

	#<pds>         = #1
	#<level>       = #2
	#<cross_t>     = #3
	#<search_from> = #4
	#<w_to>        = #5

	#<rec_count> = #[#<pds>]
	o<zdir> if [#<search_from> GE #<w_to>]
		#<z_dir> = 1
	o<zdir> else
		#<z_dir> = -1
	o<zdir> endif

	(margin a candidate must clear past search_from to count as a genuinely)
	(new interval, not a re-detection of the same joint search_from came from -)
	(deliberately larger than l_eff's own 0.001 grazing epsilon, a different)
	(purpose: that one tolerates the level exactly grazing the floor, this one)
	(has to tell "a new interval" apart from "the same point we started at")
	#<resume_margin> = [0.01 * #<_mm>]

	#<d_off> = #<cross_t>
	#<l_eff> = [#<level> + [0.001 * #<_mm>]]
	#<_pl_resume_found> = 0
	#<_pl_resume_z> = 0
	#<have_prev> = 0
	#<pz> = #[#<pds> + 1]
	#<px> = #[#<pds> + 2]
	#<scan_ptr> = [#<pds> + 9]
	#<scan_i>   = 1
	o<scan01> while [[#<scan_i> LT #<rec_count>] AND [#<_pl_resume_found> EQ 0]]
		#<scan_i> = [#<scan_i> + 1]
		#<cz> = #[#<scan_ptr>]
		#<cx> = #[#<scan_ptr> + 1]
		#<s_len> = SQRT[[#<cz> - #<pz>] * [#<cz> - #<pz>] + [#<cx> - #<px>] * [#<cx> - #<px>]]
		o<c_seg> if [#<s_len> GT 0.0001]
			(outward normal of the segment, pointing away from the material)
			#<n_z> = [#<z_dir> * [#<cx> - #<px>] / #<s_len>]
			#<n_x> = [-#<z_dir> * [#<cz> - #<pz>] / #<s_len>]
			#<q1z> = [#<pz> + #<d_off> * #<n_z>]
			#<q1x> = [#<px> + #<d_off> * #<n_x>]
			#<q2z> = [#<cz> + #<d_off> * #<n_z>]
			#<q2x> = [#<cx> + #<d_off> * #<n_x>]

			(candidate this segment/joint offers, before the past-search_from test)
			#<cand_found> = 0

			(fold-back guard: this segment's own offset start can land BEHIND)
			(where the previous segment's offset already reached - e.g. two)
			(fillet chords in quick succession at a tight corner - bridging)
			(that with a straight gap connector would read as a spurious)
			(momentary re-entry that the real, smooth profile never has. Only)
			(the GAP test is skipped when that happens; this segment's own)
			(in-segment crossing, checked just below, is still evaluated normally,)
			(since a single segment's own two ends are always forward-ordered)
			o<gap> if [#<have_prev>]
				#<q1_prog>  = [-#<z_dir> * #<q1z>]
				#<pq2_prog> = [-#<z_dir> * #<pq2z>]
				o<foldchk> if [#<q1_prog> GE [#<pq2_prog> - 0.0001]]
					o<gap_hit> if [[#<pq2x> GE #<l_eff>] AND [#<q1x> LT #<l_eff>]]
						#<cand_z> = [#<pq2z> + [#<q1z> - #<pq2z>] * [#<l_eff> - #<pq2x>] / [#<q1x> - #<pq2x>]]
						#<cand_found> = 1
					o<gap_hit> endif
				o<foldchk> endif
			o<gap> endif

			o<c_ent> if [#<cand_found>]
				(matched by the corner connector above)
			o<c_ent> elseif [[#<q1x> GE #<l_eff>] AND [#<q2x> LT #<l_eff>]]
				#<cand_z> = [#<q1z> + [#<q2z> - #<q1z>] * [#<l_eff> - #<q1x>] / [#<q2x> - #<q1x>]]
				#<cand_found> = 1
			o<c_ent> endif

			(only a candidate genuinely past search_from qualifies - this is what)
			(lets the scan keep going instead of latching on the wrong one.)
			(z_dir's sign convention matches the block-check in lathe_level_pass:)
			(z_dir times point-minus-reference is NEGATIVE for a point meaningfully)
			(further along the cut direction from the reference, not positive)
			o<qualify> if [#<cand_found>]
				o<past> if [[#<z_dir> * [#<cand_z> - #<search_from>]] LT [-#<resume_margin>]]
					#<_pl_resume_found> = 1
					#<_pl_resume_z> = #<cand_z>
				o<past> endif
			o<qualify> endif

			#<pq2z> = #<q2z>
			#<pq2x> = #<q2x>
			#<have_prev> = 1
		o<c_seg> endif
		#<pz> = #<cz>
		#<px> = #<cx>
		#<scan_ptr> = [#<scan_ptr> + 8]
	o<scan01> endwhile

	(a qualifying candidate past the window end isn't usable - nothing more)
	(to cut in THIS window, even though the profile does eventually drop again.)
	(same sign convention as the past-search_from test above: z_dir times)
	(resume_z-minus-w_to is NEGATIVE when resume_z has gone further than w_to)
	o<wclip> if [#<_pl_resume_found>]
		o<inwin> if [[#<z_dir> * [#<_pl_resume_z> - #<w_to>]] LT 0]
			#<_pl_resume_found> = 0
		o<inwin> endif
	o<wclip> endif

	(THE ENVELOPE'S OWN ANSWER, reported separately from the scan's, so that)
	(improving WHERE a level resumes cannot move WHETHER phase 1 stops here.)
	#<_pl_env_found> = 0
	#<_pl_env_z> = 0
	o<renv> if [#<_pl_res_n> GT 1]
		#<re_top> = #[#<_pl_res_base>]
		o<re_above> if [#<level> LE [#<re_top> + 0.000001]]
			#<re_i> = 0
			#<re_z> = #[#<_pl_res_base> + [#<_pl_res_n> - 1] * 2 + 1]
			o<re_w> while [#<re_i> LT [#<_pl_res_n> - 1]]
				#<re_l0> = #[#<_pl_res_base> + #<re_i> * 2]
				#<re_l1> = #[#<_pl_res_base> + [#<re_i> + 1] * 2]
				o<re_hit> if [[#<level> LE [#<re_l0> + 0.000001]] AND [#<level> GE [#<re_l1> - 0.000001]]]
					#<re_z0> = #[#<_pl_res_base> + #<re_i> * 2 + 1]
					#<re_z1> = #[#<_pl_res_base> + [#<re_i> + 1] * 2 + 1]
					o<re_lin> if [ABS[#<re_l1> - #<re_l0>] GT 0.000001]
						#<re_z> = [#<re_z0> + [#<re_z1> - #<re_z0>] * [#<level> - #<re_l0>] / [#<re_l1> - #<re_l0>]]
					o<re_lin> else
						#<re_z> = #<re_z0>
					o<re_lin> endif
					#<re_i> = #<_pl_res_n>
				o<re_hit> else
					#<re_i> = [#<re_i> + 1]
				o<re_hit> endif
			o<re_w> endwhile
			o<re_past> if [[#<z_dir> * [#<re_z> - #<search_from>]] LT [-#<resume_margin>]]
				o<re_win> if [[#<z_dir> * [#<re_z> - #<w_to>]] GE 0]
					#<_pl_env_found> = 1
					#<_pl_env_z> = #<re_z>
				o<re_win> endif
			o<re_past> endif
		o<re_above> endif
	o<renv> endif

o<lathe_level_next_start> endsub
